  "text_md": "Quantities  of one  kind  are  said  to be  inversely  proportional  to quantities of  another kind,  if  the  ratio  of any  two  of the  first kind  is equal  to  the  inverse ratio  of  the  corresponding  two  of the  other  kind.\n\n- If  6  men can do a piece  of  work  in  4  days,  then  8 men  can  do  it in 3 days,  or  6:8  equals  the  inverse  ratio  of 4:3,  7.e.5:4. Hence  the  number  of  men  required  to  do  some  work,  and  the  time  necessary  to  do  it, are inversely  proportional.\n181. Jn  any proportion  the product  of  the  means  is equal  to  the product  of  the  extremes.\n\nLet\n\nClearing  of fractions,\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n182. The  mean  proportional between  two  numbers  is equal  to' the  square  root  of  their product.\n183. If  the product  of two  numbers  is  equal  to  the  product  of two  other  numbers,  either  pair  may  be  made  the  means,  and  the other pair  the  extremes,  of  a proportion. (Converse  of  § 181.)\n\nLet  the  proportion  be a:b=6:¢.\n\nThen\n\n$$Ore Con nS aLGLe) b= Vac.$$\n\nHence\n\nIf mn  =  pq,  and  we  divide  both  members  by nq,  we  have\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nEx.  2. Determine  whether  the following  proportion  is correct or  not: 8:5=7:48.\n\n8 x  43 =  85,  and  5 x  7 =  35;  hence  the  proportion  is correct.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nor",
